know what he looks like.

126
00:08:32,520 --> 00:08:33,440
Who are you?

127
00:08:36,260 --> 00:08:37,260
Hello, Yugi.

128
00:08:37,560 --> 00:08:39,148
We've been looking for you.

129
00:08:39,740 --> 00:08:40,570
Who's we?

130
00:08:40,920 --> 00:08:43,096
You'll find out if you walk that way.

131
00:08:43,540 --> 00:08:45,757
Fifty-three steps forward
and into that tent.

132
00:08:45,840 --> 00:08:48,560
My master is waiting for you inside.

133
00:08:50,320 --> 00:08:52,460
It's in your best interest to go.

134
00:08:55,980 --> 00:08:57,740
Still no sign of Yugi.

135
00:08:58,940 --> 00:09:01,800
Hey, there he is, right there. Where?

136
00:09:04,420 --> 00:09:05,250
Yugi!

137
00:09:07,020 --> 00:09:09,200
I'm getting too old for this.

138
00:09:11,500 --> 00:09:12,860
There's no one here.

139
00:09:13,580 --> 00:09:14,600
Magic show.

140
00:09:16,080 --> 00:09:17,640
Enter here, Yugi.

141
00:09:17,960 --> 00:09:19,380
My master's waiting.

142
00:09:23,920 --> 00:09:25,040
Where'd he go?

143
00:09:26,560 --> 00:09:28,140
There he is! Yugi?

144
00:09:28,440 --> 00:09:30,660
It's almost like he's in a trance.

145
00:09:33,500 --> 00:09:34,330
Yugi!

146
00:09:37,860 --> 00:09:39,460
He's trapped in there!

147
00:09:41,080 --> 00:09:41,910
Yugi!

148
00:09:43,440 --> 00:09:44,270
Yugi!

149
00:09:44,353 --> 00:09:45,436
Yugi, where are you?

150
00:09:45,840 --> 00:09:46,840
No, he's gone!

151
00:09:48,100 --> 00:09:50,260
That's weird. Seto!

152
00:09:51,040 --> 00:09:54,637
The tournament surveillance system
just lost track of Yugi Moto.

153
00:09:54,720 --> 00:09:55,720
He's disappeared!

154
00:09:55,860 --> 00:09:57,880
He's disappeared? Impossible.

155
00:09:59,200 --> 00:10:01,940
Make sure the satellite
link is working now.

156
00:10:05,740 --> 00:10:08,900
Yugi's dual disk sends
out a constant ID signal,

157
00:10:09,100 --> 00:10:12,300
so wherever he is, his
signal's being blocked somehow.

158
00:10:12,620 --> 00:10:13,880
But I'll find him.

159
00:10:25,340 --> 00:10:26,760
Where am I?

160
00:10:28,360 --> 00:10:30,620
Hacking into Battle City database.

161
00:10:32,160 --> 00:10:34,560
Duelist profile for Yugi Moto.

162
00:10:35,100 --> 00:10:36,820
Dueling level, five stars.

163
00:10:37,220 --> 00:10:39,520
Rarest card, Dark Magician.

164
00:10:41,560 --> 00:10:43,120
My Dark Magician!

165
00:10:48,480 --> 00:10:50,009
I've been waiting for you.

166
00:10:50,320 --> 00:10:55,120
You are not worthy of having me in your
deck, so prepare to lose me forever.

167
00:10:56,800 --> 00:10:59,697
You're not the only duelist
with my power in their deck,

168
00:10:59,780 --> 00:11:01,997
Yugi, and you're certainly not the best.

169
00:11:02,080 --> 00:11:05,820
It's time that you met the true
master of the Dark Magician.

170
00:11:07,160 --> 00:11:09,180
All right, enough of these tricks.

171
00:11:13,380 --> 00:11:14,657
Welcome, Yugi Moto.

172
00:11:14,740 --> 00:11:17,540
I am the illusionist known as Arcana,

173
00:11:17,780 --> 00:11:21,020
and soon your favorite card
will be dueling for me.

174
00:11:25,120 --> 00:11:28,960
Only a true master of illusion
deserves to hold a dark magician.

175
00:11:29,500 --> 00:11:32,147
You will never understand
its full potential.

176
00:11:33,600 --> 00:11:35,460
That is enough, Arcana.

177
00:11:36,200 --> 00:11:37,200
Sorry, Yugi.

178
00:11:37,500 --> 00:11:42,206
I know it must be hard to think of your
favorite card in another duelist's deck.

179
00:11:42,360 --> 00:11:44,580
Well, I challenge you to a duel.

180
00:11:45,320 --> 00:11:48,200
The winner will take the
loser's Dark Magician.

181
00:11:48,540 --> 00:11:49,580
And I accept.

182
00:11:50,000 --> 00:11:52,597
You must know that when a
duelist builds his deck,

183
00:11:52,680 --> 00:11:56,209
he chooses his favorites from
many different types of cards.

184
00:11:56,320 --> 00:11:59,060
But sometimes a card can choose a duelist.

185
00:11:59,280 --> 00:12:03,900
The two are connected, and the duelist
can tap into the card's true power.

186
00:12:04,120 --> 00:12:06,944
Because each is bound by
the heart of the cards,

187
00:12:07,100 --> 00:12:09,980
and the Dark Magician has chosen me.

188
00:12:11,560 --> 00:12:16,560
He has never let me down, And I place
my complete trust in my dark magician.

189
00:12:19,700 --> 00:12:21,040
So it's true.

190
00:12:21,300 --> 00:12:24,476
The great Yugi Moto never
backs down from a challenge.

191
00:12:24,680 --> 00:12:25,621
Very impressive.

192
00:12:25,980 --> 00:12:28,417
But this room's a little
cramped, don't you think?

193
00:12:28,500 --> 00:12:32,440
Fortunately, I know of a special
duel ring close by. Follow me.

194
00:12:36,580 --> 00:12:37,410
Hurry.

195
00:12:37,780 --> 00:12:39,760
It's almost curtain time.

196
00:12:40,380 --> 00:12:44,800
I have special orders from my superiors
to make this a real spectacle.

197
00:12:46,220 --> 00:12:49,338
What do you mean you have
orders from your superiors?

198
00:12:49,680 --> 00:12:52,445
Just who is it that you're
working for, Arcana?

199
00:12:53,220 --> 00:12:55,160
Relax and enjoy the show.

200
00:12:55,760 --> 00:12:59,500
Forget who's backstage,
just worry about me.

201
00:13:01,780 --> 00:13:04,960
Could this deranged showman
be working for Merrick?

202
00:13:05,140 --> 00:13:09,905
If he is, then there could be much more
at stake here than just my dark magician.

203
00:13:10,280 --> 00:13:11,110
Ta-da!

204
00:13:11,193 --> 00:13:13,200
Beyond that door lies my dueling ring.

205
00:13:16,980 --> 00:13:20,000
I had it specially made for this match.

206
00:13:21,720 --> 00:13:25,073
It's almost time to raise the
curtain and start the show.

207
00:13:25,280 --> 00:13:27,640
I hope you enjoy a good matinee, Yu-Gi.

208
00:13:27,860 --> 00:13:30,036
You'll notice we're completely alone.

209
00:13:30,240 --> 00:13:32,657
There are no screaming
fans and no cameras.

210
00:13:32,740 --> 00:13:37,397
Yes, it's the perfect setting for a private
performance with so much on the line.

211
00:13:37,480 --> 00:13:40,720
We'll duel according to
Battle City Tournament rules.

212
00:13:41,080 --> 00:13:44,620
But thanks to our location, not
even Kaiba knows we're here.

213
00:13:45,840 --> 00:13:50,720
Now, let's shuffle our decks and
let the show begin, shall we?

214
00:13:51,380 --> 00:13:52,660
I'm watching you.

215
00:13:53,140 --> 00:13:55,860
Don't try any sleight of hand, Arcana.

216
00:13:56,440 --> 00:13:59,322
Card tricks are strictly
for amateurs, Yugi Moto.

217
00:13:59,540 --> 00:14:03,380
Just to be sure, I'll
cut your deck. Of course.

218
00:14:04,180 --> 00:14:08,440
You know, there is an old saying
among high rollers and card sharks.

219
00:14:08,760 --> 00:14:12,840
Always trust your opponents, but
only after you've cut their deck.

220
00:14:14,160 --> 00:14:15,042
Here's another.

221
00:14:17,100 --> 00:14:19,100
Never trust a masked man.

222
00:14:20,040 --> 00:14:21,220
I'm offended.

223
00:14:21,800 --> 00:14:23,940
Besides, you and I are a lot alike.

224
00:14:24,240 --> 00:14:25,440
We both play to win.

225
00:14:25,760 --> 00:14:27,497
Of course, in this duel performance,

226
00:14:27,580 --> 00:14:30,404
